@startuml credited-closure-enter
' ============================================================================
' One credited entry of the structural closure walk (task 7924): the work
' item Enter(r, x, c) of verify_structural_closure_in_ledger_with_credit in
' rspace++/src/rspace/persistence/closure.rs, whose counts realize the
' credited epoch of formal/rocq/stack_safe_pda/theories/CreditedClosureLedger.v.
'   GREY   #616161  the work item and the memoized path that only counts
'   BLUE   #1565C0  checks and the counting the old walk did not do
'   AMBER  #EF6C00  decisions
'   GREEN  #2E7D32  inventory growth and the credited expansion
'   RED    #C62828  refusals: each one aborts the walk, and the caller
'                   discards its ledger
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam StateBorderColor #455A64
skinparam StateFontSize 13
skinparam NoteBorderColor #455A64

title <b>One credited entry of the closure walk</b>\ncounts move only by credit, and children are credited only by the domains that crossed

state "Enter(r, x, c)" as Enter #E0E0E0 : reference <latex>r</latex>, expectation <latex>x</latex>,\ncredit <latex>c \subseteq \{\mathrm{Current}, \mathrm{Retained}\}</latex>
state "Admit the visit" as Admit #BBDEFB : first visit in the epoch: distinct-object\nand byte limits; declared-length check
state "Count the credit" as Count #BBDEFB : for each <latex>d \in c</latex>: <latex>C_d(r) \leftarrow C_d(r) + 1</latex>, checked\n<latex>\kappa = \{\, d \in c \mid C_d(r) = 0 \text{ before} \,\}</latex>
state "Expectation verified\nin this epoch?" as Memo #FFE0B2
state "Store the counts" as Store #E0E0E0 : no expansion, no read
state "Cycle check" as Cycle #FFE0B2 : is <latex>r</latex> active in this epoch?
state "Grow the inventories" as Grow #C8E6C9 : <latex>\mathrm{Retained} \in \kappa</latex>: union limits, then <latex>O_U + 1</latex>, <latex>B_U + w(r)</latex>\n<latex>\mathrm{Current} \in \kappa</latex>: <latex>O_L + 1</latex>, <latex>B_L + w(r)</latex>
state "Load and parse" as Load #BBDEFB : bounded read, length and digest check,\nkind and context validation
state "Expand with credit κ" as Expand #A5D6A7 : push Exit(r, x), then one Enter(t, x', <latex>\kappa</latex>)\nper outgoing reference occurrence t
state "Refused" as Refused #FFCDD2 : UnexpandedClosureCrossing, ObjectCycle,\nResourceLimit, CounterOverflow, or a load error

[*] --> Enter
Enter --> Admit
Admit -[#C62828]-> Refused : limit or length
Admit -[#1565C0]-> Count
Count -[#C62828]-> Refused : CounterOverflow
Count -[#EF6C00]-> Memo
Memo -[#616161]-> Store : yes, <latex>\kappa = \varnothing</latex>
Memo -[#C62828]-> Refused : yes, <latex>\kappa \ne \varnothing</latex>
Memo -[#EF6C00]-> Cycle : no
Cycle -[#C62828]-> Refused : ObjectCycle
Cycle -[#2E7D32]-> Grow : acyclic so far
Grow -[#C62828]-> Refused : union limit
Grow -[#1565C0]-> Load
Load -[#C62828]-> Refused : load or format error
Load -[#2E7D32]-> Expand
Store --> [*]
Expand --> [*]

note right of Enter #E3F2FD
  The epoch's root: <latex>R_d(m) \leftarrow R_d(m) + 1</latex> for each <latex>d \in D</latex>,
  then Enter(<latex>m</latex>, Manifest, <latex>D</latex>). Callers choose <latex>D</latex>:
  cold current state: Current and Retained;
  each historical state and the successor inventory: Retained.
end note

note left of Expand #F1F8E9
  On a quiescent predecessor, the first entry of an object
  whose count in <latex>d</latex> is zero carries <latex>d</latex>, so every crossing
  happens at a first visit, which always expands:
  the yes, <latex>\kappa \ne \varnothing</latex> refusal never fires. After the epoch
  <latex>C'_d(v) = C_d(v) + \mathrm{occ}([m])(v) + I(\kappa_d, v)</latex>.
end note
@enduml
